      "text": "57-year-old male presenting with headache with dizziness for 1 days. Character: throbbing at the back of the head; radiation: it does not spread; aggravated by morning time; relieved by rest. Severity 5/10. Associated: blurred vision, palpitations. PMH: Hypertension for 8 years; Appendectomy in 1996. Drugs: Amlodipine 5 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: diabetes. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
